>
  <p>
    <strong>The short version:</strong> a private RPC protects the submission path: your
    transaction skips the public mempool, so attackers cannot see it pending. A batch auction
    changes the execution model: no pending transaction exists, everything clears at a uniform
    price, and an enforced signed limit replaces the slippage tolerance. The first hides the
    target; the second removes it. They cover different layers and combine cleanly.
  </p>

